1
00:00:33,719 --> 00:00:34,340
Like it?

2
00:00:35,399 --> 00:00:37,259
I bought this from down south.

3
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:39,579
It's nothing like the ones

4
00:00:39,719 --> 00:00:40,340
you buy at the department store.

5
00:00:43,140 --> 00:00:44,039
If you like it, take it.

6
00:00:47,299 --> 00:00:47,759
No thanks.

7
00:00:50,159 --> 00:00:51,880
I've got plenty of this stuff anyway.

8
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:53,259
Besides,

9
00:00:53,759 --> 00:00:55,539
I'm moving out of this pigeon coop soon.

10
00:00:57,200 --> 00:00:59,079
You're marrying Biao?

11
00:01:00,600 --> 00:01:01,439
Pretty much.

12
00:01:02,119 --> 00:01:03,060
He told me

13
00:01:03,340 --> 00:01:04,480
to quit my job

14
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:05,599
and be the boss lady.

15
00:01:06,739 --> 00:01:07,579
For real?

16
00:01:07,680 --> 00:01:08,700
You said yes?

17
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:10,379
You can't do that.

18
00:01:11,040 --> 00:01:11,879
When it comes to men,

19
00:01:12,299 --> 00:01:13,840
you can't let them have it that easy.

20
00:01:14,579 --> 00:01:15,319
Besides,

21
00:01:15,719 --> 00:01:17,620
if it's too easy, they won't cherish it.

22
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:18,980
You've got to string them along.

23
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:20,799
Make him feel like

24
00:01:20,859 --> 00:01:21,980
his heart is being clawed at.

25
00:01:22,420 --> 00:01:23,140
Craving it,

26
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:24,260
yearning for it,

27
00:01:24,540 --> 00:01:25,260
but just out of reach.

28
00:01:25,859 --> 00:01:27,500
That's how you make him treat you right.

29
00:01:27,959 --> 00:01:30,340
Couples shouldn't be class enemies.

30
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,319
Why play so many mind games?

31
00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:34,319
Isn't being honest better?

32
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:37,680
Fine, fine.

33
00:01:37,859 --> 00:01:39,180
Your Zhuzi is the best.

34
00:01:39,359 --> 00:01:40,579
Scraping by on that dead salary—

35
00:01:40,819 --> 00:01:41,819
what's the point?

36
00:01:42,060 --> 00:01:43,299
I really don't get what you see in him.

37
00:01:44,840 --> 00:01:46,060
What... what's wrong with Zhuzi?

38
00:01:47,079 --> 00:01:49,439
He's an honest worker, okay?

39
00:01:49,799 --> 00:01:51,719
Pure-hearted, earning his own keep.

40
00:01:52,299 --> 00:01:54,560
None of those sleazy street schemes.

41
00:01:55,099 --> 00:01:56,239
What's wrong with the streets?

42
00:01:56,439 --> 00:01:58,140
Street hustlers actually make good money!

43
00:01:58,799 --> 00:01:59,500
Besides,

44
00:01:59,719 --> 00:02:01,780
he deals with street thugs all the time.

45
00:02:02,719 --> 00:02:03,959
The other day by the factory gate,

46
00:02:04,079 --> 00:02:05,560
he got into a bloody brawl.

47
00:02:06,099 --> 00:02:07,379
A hothead like him,

48
00:02:07,959 --> 00:02:08,840
how could he ever compare to my Biao,

49
00:02:08,979 --> 00:02:10,800
a real businessman?

50
00:02:12,740 --> 00:02:14,460
I know exactly what kind of man he is.

51
00:02:14,659 --> 00:02:15,599
Nobody can tell me otherwise.

52
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:20,400
So much for my good intentions.

53
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:24,020
Xiu'er!

54
00:02:24,979 --> 00:02:25,400
Xiu'er!

55
00:02:26,280 --> 00:02:26,560
Coming! Coming!

56
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:27,159
Let's go, let's go.

57
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:31,659
Mengmeng, we're taking off!

58
00:03:35,060 --> 00:03:35,520
Come on.

59
00:03:36,139 --> 00:03:37,099
I don't know how!

60
00:03:37,360 --> 00:03:38,500
Sis, I really don't know how.

61
00:03:38,759 --> 00:03:39,919
It's fine.

62
00:03:40,060 --> 00:03:42,219
You really can dance. I never noticed.

63
00:03:42,419 --> 00:03:43,340
I'll teach you.

64
00:03:45,419 --> 00:03:47,419
So this is the Little sis you talk about?

65
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:48,120
Yeah.

66
00:03:49,180 --> 00:03:50,340
Welcome, Little sis!

67
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:51,099
Hi, Biao.

68
00:03:51,479 --> 00:03:53,280
Whenever you come here, it's on the house.

69
00:03:54,419 --> 00:03:55,419
Sure, thanks!

70
00:03:58,180 --> 00:03:59,280
See? Isn't that great?

71
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:01,539
He's such a great dancer, Hong.

72
00:04:12,659 --> 00:04:13,180
Come on, Hong'er.

73
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,860
I've been waiting up here forever.

74
00:04:23,699 --> 00:04:25,300
It was packed downstairs today, you know.

75
00:04:25,699 --> 00:04:26,339
I'm exhausted.

76
00:04:29,399 --> 00:04:30,680
If you ask me,

77
00:04:31,139 --> 00:04:33,600
quit that shipyard job.

78
00:04:34,379 --> 00:04:35,639
I mean, my woman

79
00:04:35,740 --> 00:04:36,879
shouldn't have to work out there.

80
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:42,060
Nobody's got what you've got, Biao.

81
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,199
You,

82
00:04:45,379 --> 00:04:46,800
you come be the lady boss.

83
00:04:46,939 --> 00:04:47,579
Really?

84
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:48,980
What about the folks downstairs?

85
00:04:49,220 --> 00:04:49,959
You'll be in charge of all of them.

86
00:04:53,740 --> 00:04:54,500
Biao,

87
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:56,360
Xiu'er is here too.

88
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,519
Xiu'er came up, too.

89
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:04,339
Xiu'er,

90
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,459
come on in.

91
00:05:08,680 --> 00:05:09,259
Come on, Xiu'er.

92
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:11,420
Sit down.

93
00:05:11,639 --> 00:05:12,399
Hello, Biao.

94
00:05:13,339 --> 00:05:14,839
Ah, Xiu'er's here.

95
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:18,220
Sit, sit.

96
00:05:18,399 --> 00:05:19,379
Make yourself at home.

97
00:05:20,779 --> 00:05:21,720
Thank you, Biao.

98
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,699
Look how pretty my Xiu'er is.

99
00:05:25,480 --> 00:05:27,360
Hook her up with a job, will you?

100
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,139
Biao,

101
00:05:29,279 --> 00:05:32,259
I can pour tea, serve drinks, whatever.

102
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,120
You're already the lady boss.

103
00:05:37,300 --> 00:05:38,959
Why even ask me about this?

104
00:05:40,040 --> 00:05:41,680
Xiu'er is like our own sister.

105
00:05:42,120 --> 00:05:43,459
Why bother with hard work?

106
00:05:43,740 --> 00:05:44,579
Just come have fun.

107
00:05:45,819 --> 00:05:46,560
Tell you what, Xiu'er.

108
00:05:47,399 --> 00:05:48,740
Come dance here for me.

109
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:50,459
Dance your heart out.

110
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:53,079
I'll pay you two yuan a day.

111
00:05:54,300 --> 00:05:55,079
Two yuan?

112
00:05:57,279 --> 00:05:59,360
Thanks, Biao. Thanks, Hong.

113
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:02,139
Can you drink?

114
00:06:04,439 --> 00:06:05,279
Drink?

115
00:06:06,139 --> 00:06:06,860
Not really.

116
00:06:15,279 --> 00:06:15,980
No worries.

117
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:18,480
You can learn.

118
00:06:19,459 --> 00:06:20,459
If you can drink a bit,

119
00:06:20,980 --> 00:06:22,720
I'll give you three yuan a day.

120
00:06:24,819 --> 00:06:25,459
Xiu'er,

121
00:06:25,779 --> 00:06:26,620
take it, quick.

122
00:06:26,899 --> 00:06:28,139
My booze is all top-shelf.

123
00:06:28,199 --> 00:06:28,819
It's fine.

124
00:06:29,500 --> 00:06:30,199
Come on, drink up.

125
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:48,939
He.

126
00:06:49,759 --> 00:06:50,300
Around here,

127
00:06:50,379 --> 00:06:52,300
your wanted poster is still up.

128
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:55,120
The cops know your face all too well.

129
00:06:55,899 --> 00:06:57,600
If they find out you're here,

130
00:06:57,959 --> 00:06:59,980
wouldn't that make things tricky?

131
00:07:07,579 --> 00:07:08,279
Threatening me?

132
00:07:15,139 --> 00:07:17,180
What are we missing here?

133
00:07:21,459 --> 00:07:22,800
Scared the hell out of me, boss!

134
00:07:22,879 --> 00:07:24,199
Why do you walk so quietly?

135
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,439
What're you scared of? Afraid of me?

136
00:07:26,879 --> 00:07:28,220
Got a guilty conscience, do you?

137
00:07:29,040 --> 00:07:29,980
No way.

138
00:07:30,579 --> 00:07:32,019
It's not like I stole your braised pork.

139
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:33,600
Out with it.

140
00:07:34,879 --> 00:07:35,800
What did you figure out?

141
00:07:37,319 --> 00:07:38,360
Look here, boss.

142
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:40,560
All the routes in and out of Songliao

143
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:41,800
are locked down by us.

144
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:43,779
That proves only one thing:

145
00:07:44,379 --> 00:07:46,160
those goods never left at all.

146
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:47,459
Nine times out of ten,

147
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:49,019
they're still hidden somewhere in town.

148
00:07:51,300 --> 00:07:52,480
Go rat me out to the cops then.

149
00:07:56,319 --> 00:07:57,240
What are you talking about?

150
00:07:57,339 --> 00:07:59,240
I'm genuinely looking out for you.

151
00:07:59,620 --> 00:08:00,519
Didn't I just say?

152
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:01,839
We're still supposed to

153
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,439
do some business together.

154
00:08:04,300 --> 00:08:05,220
I'm not going anywhere.

155
00:08:06,339 --> 00:08:07,100
I just think

156
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,139
your place is pretty good.

157
00:08:10,459 --> 00:08:11,420
I'll just stay right here with you,

158
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:13,399
laying low.

159
00:08:14,439 --> 00:08:14,980
And then?

160
00:08:16,540 --> 00:08:17,360
Wait till the heat dies down.

161
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:19,139
What if the heat

162
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,560
doesn't blow over anytime soon?

163
00:08:21,079 --> 00:08:22,399
Exactly my point.

164
00:08:22,639 --> 00:08:24,139
That's the fishy part.

165
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:26,199
I think there are two possibilities.

166
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,100
Either

167
00:08:27,399 --> 00:08:28,740
we're checking too strictly

168
00:08:28,899 --> 00:08:29,680
and they can't move the goods out,

169
00:08:30,319 --> 00:08:30,860
or

170
00:08:31,399 --> 00:08:33,340
they've got another plan in motion.

171
00:08:34,460 --> 00:08:35,200
Here, He.

172
00:08:41,659 --> 00:08:43,059
He, I've always been curious.

173
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:44,940
I heard

174
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:46,960
you went back and forth via Shanhai Pass,

175
00:08:47,120 --> 00:08:48,240
moving people over a dozen times,

176
00:08:48,559 --> 00:08:49,799
and never got caught once.

177
00:08:51,740 --> 00:08:53,120
Which route did you take?

178
00:08:59,179 --> 00:08:59,940
What do you want to move?

179
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,940
I'm just running a small hustle.

180
00:09:03,399 --> 00:09:04,279
Moving some cargo.

181
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,100
I just figured,

182
00:09:06,639 --> 00:09:07,840
an extra safe route...

183
00:09:08,059 --> 00:09:09,080
Wouldn't that be better?

184
00:09:11,419 --> 00:09:12,059
Looks like

185
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:14,159
we can't squeeze thieves too tight.

186
00:09:14,600 --> 00:09:15,320
We gotta give them some slack.

187
00:09:15,600 --> 00:09:16,379
With a little slack,

188
00:09:17,059 --> 00:09:19,080
we might get an unexpected catch.

189
00:09:20,899 --> 00:09:21,460
He,

190
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:24,019
having the same dish gets old.

191
00:09:25,179 --> 00:09:26,200
Hey, Cui'er.

192
00:09:29,279 --> 00:09:30,000
Come on over.

193
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:30,799
Hurry up, girl.

194
00:09:37,159 --> 00:09:38,840
Come on, over here.

195
00:09:46,539 --> 00:09:47,100
This one's nice.

196
00:09:47,179 --> 00:09:48,419
This one's easy to handle.

197
00:09:57,139 --> 00:09:58,399
Spring Festival was just around the corner.

198
00:09:58,799 --> 00:10:01,139
The liveliest time of year for workers.

199
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:02,659
Zhou Meng and I made plans

200
00:10:02,919 --> 00:10:04,559
and came to the workers' dance social.

201
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:05,840
I guess this counted as a date.

202
00:10:06,379 --> 00:10:07,480
Yet deep down,

203
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:09,960
something just feels off.

204
00:10:10,039 --> 00:10:10,820
What's wrong?

205
00:10:13,679 --> 00:10:14,500
Well...

206
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:16,240
I've been wondering these past few days.

207
00:10:16,779 --> 00:10:18,519
Why did Ma Limin see you on his trip?

208
00:10:19,639 --> 00:10:20,240
I don't know.

209
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:22,100
Why bring him up?

210
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,259
If he's harassing you,

211
00:10:24,299 --> 00:10:24,860
tell me.

212
00:10:25,559 --> 00:10:26,120
I... I...

213
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:27,879
I don't give a damn if he's the director.

214
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,559
Watch me Kick his ass!

215
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,220
Are you done?

216
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,759
Why keep bringing him up?

217
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,039
I said it out loud in front of everyone.

218
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:36,919
The two of us

219
00:10:38,019 --> 00:10:38,879
are dating.

220
00:10:39,779 --> 00:10:41,059
So who would dare pick on me?

221
00:10:41,379 --> 00:10:41,779
Who?

222
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:49,559
How are we supposed to date?

223
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:54,580
Isn't this...

224
00:10:55,019 --> 00:10:56,240
aren't we dating right now?

225
00:10:58,279 --> 00:10:59,600
We're on a date, aren't we?

226
00:11:00,659 --> 00:11:01,139
Well, in that case...

227
00:11:01,919 --> 00:11:03,820
Wish I hadn't invited Ziwen and the guys.

228
00:11:04,139 --> 00:11:04,779
Right?

229
00:11:12,320 --> 00:11:13,080
Don't... don't do that.

230
00:11:13,500 --> 00:11:13,840
You're so annoying!

231
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:14,460
No, wait.

232
00:11:14,919 --> 00:11:16,039
Come to my place when we're done here.

233
00:11:16,519 --> 00:11:17,080
Pervert!

234
00:11:18,039 --> 00:11:18,480
Wait, no...

235
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,000
Well, look who we have here.

236
00:11:29,259 --> 00:11:31,639
If it isn't hero Liu and gorgeous Zhou!

237
00:11:32,120 --> 00:11:33,840
Came here to get all lovey-dovey?

238
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:36,620
Hey, Laizi.

239
00:11:36,879 --> 00:11:38,460
Didn't that slap hurt enough?

240
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:39,620
Want another one on the other side?

241
00:11:40,639 --> 00:11:41,200
Go ahead, hit me.

242
00:11:41,779 --> 00:11:42,159
Come on.

243
00:11:42,379 --> 00:11:43,899
Conquer with your windmill punches!

244
00:11:44,179 --> 00:11:45,840
My uncle was spot on about you.

245
00:11:46,059 --> 00:11:47,279
A hopeless case.

246
00:11:48,460 --> 00:11:49,200
Say that again!

247
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:50,720
Alright, that's enough.

248
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:51,679
Look at him.

249
00:11:52,259 --> 00:11:53,220
He's not right in the head.

250
00:11:53,539 --> 00:11:54,639
He's not worth hitting.

251
00:11:56,679 --> 00:11:57,919
Look at you two acting all tough.

252
00:11:58,039 --> 00:11:58,679
Hit me if you've got the guts!

253
00:11:58,860 --> 00:11:59,200
Come on!

254
00:11:59,419 --> 00:12:00,080
Come on, drifter!

255
00:12:00,419 --> 00:12:01,139
Talking trash to me?

256
00:12:01,620 --> 00:12:03,059
Are you seriously sick in the head?

257
00:12:05,059 --> 00:12:05,679
What do you want?

258
00:12:10,399 --> 00:12:11,740
Bro, you dropped your money.

259
00:12:22,840 --> 00:12:24,299
Look at all this trash crowding in here.

260
00:12:26,019 --> 00:12:27,379
Bro, you smell that?

261
00:12:27,779 --> 00:12:28,879
Where's that stench coming from?

262
00:12:29,519 --> 00:12:29,940
Stinks.

263
00:12:30,639 --> 00:12:31,879
Heard you spewing shit from a mile away.

264
00:12:39,519 --> 00:12:40,340
Haven't picked it all up yet.

265
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,820
Giving up a good factory job...

266
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:51,220
...just to run with these thugs?

267
00:12:52,059 --> 00:12:52,940
Seriously, Liu Haizhu, Zhou Meng.

268
00:12:53,059 --> 00:12:54,799
You two are really going downhill.

269
00:12:57,259 --> 00:12:57,860
What's that supposed to mean?

270
00:13:03,899 --> 00:13:05,480
Who do you think you're mocking?

271
00:13:06,360 --> 00:13:07,259
Not enough, huh?

272
00:13:07,899 --> 00:13:08,320
Fine.

273
00:13:17,679 --> 00:13:18,559
Playing that game, huh?

274
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:25,360
Who turns down money these days?

275
00:13:28,740 --> 00:13:29,919
Someone's out of their damn mind.

276
00:13:32,460 --> 00:13:33,019
This...

277
00:13:33,659 --> 00:13:34,879
Who turns down cash?

278
00:14:00,580 --> 00:14:01,039
Zhuzi,

279
00:14:02,159 --> 00:14:02,759
See that?

280
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:04,899
Everyone has their price.

281
00:14:05,220 --> 00:14:06,059
Some are cheap,

282
00:14:06,799 --> 00:14:07,960
bending over for a few bucks.

283
00:14:09,019 --> 00:14:09,799
Some are tougher,

284
00:14:10,539 --> 00:14:11,399
so you gotta size 'em up differently.

285
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:13,860
To bring a man to his knees,

286
00:14:14,299 --> 00:14:15,700
you don't always need your fists.

287
00:14:16,080 --> 00:14:17,759
Why'd you give him all that cash?

288
